pen","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:cancelDelete"],"scenario":"in a live headless sway session: open the menu, press Delete on an app row, run `omarchy-menu-select` (or `omarchy-shell shell summon omarchy.menu` with a select payload), then press Enter: the select caller receives the highlighted option, the confirmation is gone and no desktop file is removed"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The test and the harness run the real handler bodies under node vm with Qt.callLater run synchronously. In Qt, cancelDelete() (Menu.qml:865) and openDmenu() (Menu.qml:948) each queue keyCatcher.forceActiveFocus() for later, and the dialog's own focus handling lives in ConfirmDialog.qml. Both queue the same target, so the order should not matter, but no test in this package drives the summon through real IPC in a running shell and presses a key afterwards.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":865},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":948},{"id":"shell/Ui/ConfirmDialog.qml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-VJR1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: on a real Quickshell, does the next key after a summon over the confirmation reach the new prompt?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Live summon over a raised uninstall confirmation\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:open"],"scenario":"with the confirmation raised on the root menu, summon the root route again (keybind pressed twice): the confirmation closes and nothing is removed; pressing Delete again raises it again"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"A second press of the menu keybind sends a route summon for the current menu. With the PR it cancels the pending confirmation like any other summon, so the user must pres